  "final_text": "I finished all four steps and checked each result by reading it back from Kibana.\n\n**1. Data view:** 'Kibana Sample Data Flights' (id `d3d7af60-4c81-11e8-b3d7-01146121b73d`, index `kibana_sample_data_flights`). Its time field is **`timestamp`**. The other fields are:\n- **Text (keyword):** Carrier, Dest, DestAirportID, DestCityName, DestCountry, DestRegion, DestWeather, FlightDelayType, FlightNum, FlightTimeHour, Origin, OriginAirportID, OriginCityName, OriginCountry, OriginRegion, OriginWeather\n- **Numbers:** AvgTicketPrice, DistanceKilometers, DistanceMiles, FlightDelayMin, FlightTimeMin, dayOfWeek, hour_of_day\n- **True/false:** Cancelled, FlightDelay\n- **Locations:** DestLocation, OriginLocation\n\n**2. Dashboard:** I created 'S4-5b528e7b Flights' (id `24ce978c-e51a-4b58-8115-8a85d0249fd5`) on that data view. It has exactly two panels:\n- a line chart of the number of flights over time, using `timestamp`;\n- a bar chart of the number of flights for each of the top 10 carriers.\n\nThe dashboard opens on the last 7 days by default.\n\n**3. Alert rule:** I created 'S4-5b528e7b Cancelled flights' (id `d4429672-c7aa-410f-877a-ec4150dcc0e7`). It runs every minute, counts flights with `Cancelled:true` over the last 5 minutes using `timestamp`, and fires when the count is more than 10. It was enabled when created, so I didn't need to enable it. It has no actions attached, so it will fire but won't send notifications anywhere.\n\n**4. Edit and check:** I renamed the carrier panel to 'Flights by carrier'. Reading the dashboard back shows that title and still exactly two panels. Reading the rule back shows it is enabled, and its first run finished with status `ok`.\n\nTIME_FIELD: timestamp\nRULE_ENABLED: yes",
